	<!--
		Suppressions are accepted-with-tracking risks, not "make CI green" hacks.
		Each entry MUST include:
		  - notes: rationale + reachability assessment
		  - the precise CVE id list (one <cve> per CVE)
		  - a tightly scoped <packageUrl> or <filePath> matcher
		  - an `until` expiry; renew explicitly

		The build in `env-deploy` fails on CVSS >= 7 (HIGH/CRITICAL) for any
		non-suppressed finding. Suppress only after writing down WHY the issue
		does not (currently) translate into actual risk for our users.
	-->

	<!-- ============================================================
	     Vendored Mozilla NSS toolkit (certutil + libs) from 2010
	     ============================================================
	     `afirma-ui-simple-configurator/src/main/resources/{windows,linux,osx}/certutil.<os>.zip`
	     ships a 2010-era Mozilla NSS distribution (certutil.exe, freebl3, libnspr4,
	     nss3, nssckbi, nssdbm3, softokn3, sqlite3, ssl3, smime3) used during the
	     post-install configurator to register the Autofirma trust root in the
	     Mozilla NSS database (Firefox / Thunderbird).

	     Reachability assessment for the bundled sqlite3.dll CVEs:
	       - The DLL is invoked exclusively by certutil.exe, locally, against the
	         user's own NSS profile DB. There is no SQL surface exposed to network
	         input, attacker-controlled file, or remote untrusted data.
	       - Trigger conditions for the listed SQLite CVEs require a malicious SQL
	         statement or a crafted database. The configurator does neither: it
	         only adds certificates with `certutil -A` and mostly-fixed args.
	       - The configurator runs once at install / uninstall time, then the
	         binary is no longer executed.
	       - Replacement is tracked under M3 (modernise NSS toolkit / replace
	         vendored 2010 binary with current NSS or remove the embedded toolkit
	         in favour of system NSS). See plan at
	         ~/.claude/plans/haz-esto-1-cumplir-cozy-bachman.md (M3).

	     Suppression scope: the embedded sqlite3.dll only. The other DLLs in the
	     same archive (nss3, softokn3, etc.) are checked separately.

	     Reviewer: <name pending>, 2026-05-07.
	     Renews: 2026-12-31. If still suppressed at renewal, escalate to release
	     gate hold.
	-->
	<suppress until="2026-12-31Z">
		<notes><![CDATA[
			Vendored sqlite3.dll bundled inside certutil.<os>.zip (Mozilla NSS 2010 toolkit
			used by the post-install configurator). Local-only invocation surface; CVEs
			require attacker-controlled SQL or DB. Tracked for replacement in roadmap M3.
		]]></notes>
		<filePath regex="true">.*certutil\.(windows|linux|osx)\.zip[\\/]+certutil[\\/]+sqlite3\.dll</filePath>
